  "query_preview": "..The center of the high pressure at 500 mb is now \nover the New Mexico/Arizona border and will continue to wobble\nwestward slightly through Friday. This setup will support low- \ngrade monsoon activity as subtropical moisture is prevented from \nmoving into northern AZ and the potential for a cap to develop. \nThe overall forecast reflects this idea, maintaining daily \nisolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms mostly along the \nhigh terrain. With the reduction in moisture and above normal \nheights at 500 mb, heat will be the primary concern. The lower \nelevations of the Grand Canyon and the lower elevations of Yavapai\ncounty will have Extreme Heat Warnings in effect today through \nFriday evening.\n\nFor Saturday through Tuesday, long term ensemble guidance support\nthat the high shifting back to the east while a deep trough \napproaches from the west. This could be a fairly active setup, and\nthe forecast calls for a 30-70% chance of precipitation across \nmost of northern AZ each day. This could support scattered to \nnumerous showers and thunderstorms. There is still plenty of room \nfor the details to change, and we will be watching this period \nclosely with future forecast updates.",
